# Build & commit workflow

## Gulp tasks

| Task | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `setup-hooks` | Copy `pre-commit` / `post-commit` into `.git/hooks/` (executable) |
| `rename-js` | Always rename `scripts-*.js` and update HTML refs |
| `rename-js-if-changed` | Rename + update HTML only if `assets/js/scripts-*.js` changed |
| `precommit` | Used by git hook: `rename-js-if-changed` + version bump when JS changed |
| `serve` (default) | BrowserSync on `./`, watches HTML/CSS/JS |
| `update-html` | Sync HTML script refs to current JS filename (no rename) |

## Commit hooks

`pre-commit` → runs `yarn precommit` (`gulp precommit`):
1. If `assets/js/scripts-*.js` has no git changes → skip (no rename, no version bump)
2. Otherwise `rename-js` (timestamp rename + update all HTML refs)
3. `yarn version patch -i`
4. Stages generated changes

`post-commit` → amends commit to include any remaining staged hook output.

## Rules for agents

- **Never** manually edit `package.json` version
- **Never** manually change `scripts-{timestamp}.js` filename or HTML script `src`
- After JS changes, verify with `yarn start` before committing
- Use `yarn ci` (`yarn install --immutable`) in CI; `yarn verify` checks install integrity (`--immutable --check-cache`)

## Adding dependencies

Dev-only tooling belongs in `devDependencies`. Pin exact versions (`save-exact=true` in `.npmrc`).
